  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_019 (multimodal, multi-profile, PCA-2000, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted; acc 0.639). We know avgpool > transformer, weighted > concat, multi-profile > single-profile, and multimodal > RNA-only. However, the RNA encoder choice in the multimodal setting is under-explored: PCA-2000 (linear variance capture) outperformed scGPT in RNA-only (0.591 vs 0.530), but scVI (a variational autoencoder learning a latent biological representation) has not been tested in any setting. Question: Does a learned nonlinear latent encoder (scVI) provide complementary information to the image modality that PCA's linear projection misses, potentially improving on 0.639? Rationale: config_031 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA-2000 to scVI_n200 while holding all other parameters at their empirically best values (multi-profile, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted). This is a clean single-variable test that reduces uncertainty about whether the RNA encoder's representational style matters in the multimodal context, and it avoids repeating any prior configuration. If scVI matches or beats PCA, it opens a new optimization axis; if it underperforms, we confirm PCA is optimal and can redirect budget to other levers."
}

